; The numeric plane fires nothing. That is the claim, and the call count is the
; whole proof: one prompt, and all the arithmetic beside it is free.
;
; `$` assembles and so adds, `^` is the inverse so subtraction needs no glyph,
; and `[M]` folds. The quantity is interpolated INTO the prompt, which is the
; crossing back out — the expectation names the arithmetic, so a plane that
; silently contributed nothing here could not pass.
; expect: calls 1
; expect: clean
; expect: contains alpha 14
; expect: answers
($ "Answer with exactly the word: alpha"
   " " |([sum] ($ 2 3) ($ 10 (^ 3)) (/ 9 38))|)
